{"step":3,"model":"Ornith-9B-ft","prompt":"","response":"The issue is that `TIME(0,30,0)` subtracts 30 minutes but when the result goes below midnight, Excel wraps it to a date 1899-12-29. The correct approach is to use `MOD(B2-TIME(0,30,0),1)` to wrap around midnight, and wrap the whole thing in `IF(AND(A2=\"\",B2=\"\"),\"\",...)` to handle blank cells.\n\nLet me write the script:\n\n","input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"latency_ms":4489,"error":null,"tool":"write_file","tool_input":{"content":"import openpyxl\n\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('init.xlsx')\nws = wb['Sheet1']\n\nfor r in range(2, 101):\n    ws.cell(r, 3).value = f'=IF(AND(A{r}=\"\",B{r}=\"\"),\"\",MOD(B{r}-TIME(0,30,0),1))'\n\nwb.save('output.xlsx')\nprint(\"done\")\n","filePath":"/workspace/task/write_answer.py"},"tool_output":{"existed":false,"path":"/workspace/task/write_answer.py"}}
